plasmashell's thumbnails of windows (the task manager's tooltips) import each
PipeWire frame's dma-buf on the render thread, after the frame's buffer went
back to the producer.  A window that keeps resizing makes the stream
renegotiate all the time: PipeWire then removed the buffer and closed its
fds before the import ("dmabuf import failed: Bad file descriptor",
EGL_BAD_ALLOC), or the fds were reused by other files, and plasmashell's
heap was corrupted right after (the research's nested desktop, 2026-10-08).
The item now imports its own copies of the frame's fds, at the frame's own
size rather than the size negotiated last.

From the research (virtio-gpu-desktop patches/kpipewire, set k2), for
KPipeWire 6.7.91; applies to 6.7.5 unchanged.

--- a/src/pipewiresourceitem.cpp	2026-09-24 13:29:59.000000000 +0200
+++ b/src/pipewiresourceitem.cpp	2026-10-08 22:04:01.578035162 +0200
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 #include <qpa/qplatformnativeinterface.h>
 
 #include <EGL/eglext.h>
+#include <cstring>
 #include <fcntl.h>
 #include <libdrm/drm_fourcc.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
